{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790984975,"nonce":"KLDGesb/lKzCu6qi9NXOLQauPFE=","message":"Fixed in 6fdb6c9f.\n\nAll five, plus two things found while verifying:\n\n1. Scoop is tip-centred: max(box, -superellipse(|q|/r)). Note |q|, not a\nclamp: the disc is centred on the tip and extends outside the box, so the\nquadrant is mirrored. Clamping to max(-q,0) gets the silhouette right and the\ndistance wrong just outside the corner.\n2. The border fast path now bypasses when corner_n \u003c 0, and a concave corner\ntakes the offset SDF. With asymmetric widths it offsets by the smaller one;\nthe existing asymmetric branch insets the corner RADIUS, which means nothing\nfor a scoop. The notch shaders already always took the SDF branch.\n3. Normalised by the norm's gradient length. Two corrections to the proposed\nform: the convex branch must clamp t to max(qa,0), since abs() mirrors the arc\ninto the straight-inner region where it overrides the box and produced a slope\nof 3.8 at the inner centre; and the norm has to be evaluated with the largest\ncomponent factored out, because tx^p + ty^p underflows f32 at p = 8, making f\nzero, the gradient term infinite and the distance -0.\n4. Notch is max(box, -sd_box(-qa)), which gives root-2 one unit diagonally\ninside the step corner where the bar union gave 1.\n5. The factored norm removes the pow(0,0) hazard; the bevel keeps its own\nexact branch rather than going through p = 1.\n\nApplied to all NINE copies, not the three the issue named: the _dt and _vb\nvariants each carry their own, and were byte-identical before this.\n\nVerification is a Rust port at crates/blinc_gpu/tests/sdf_shaped_rect.rs, kept\nas the executable spec. Eight tests: unit gradient where the field is smooth,\nbounded slope, border-offset consistency, finiteness, and one per shape. Each\nwas checked against the ORIGINAL formulas to confirm it fails -- the bevel test\nreports 'border would be -29% off', matching the ~30% in this issue. An earlier\nversion of the gradient test passed on the broken field because it gated on\n|grad| being near 1, which skipped exactly the defective points; it now\ndiscriminates creases by forward and backward differences diverging in\nDIRECTION instead.\n\nnaga validates all nine, the HLSL cross-compile through dxc passes, and 1407\nworkspace tests pass. Not yet verified on a GPU visually.","files":null}]}